# GitHub Linguist overrides.
#
# Linguist maps *.g to GAP (see languages.yml), so without this the repo reads
# as ~60% GAP. Gata is not a Linguist-recognised language, and getting it added
# upstream requires evidence of use across ~200 unique repositories, so the best
# available option is to borrow a grammar for highlighting and stay out of the
# language statistics rather than claim a language we are not.
#
# linguist-language  -> picks the TextMate grammar used to highlight blobs/diffs
# linguist-detectable -> whether the files count toward the language bar
#
# Swift is the closest grammar by keyword overlap with Gata: func, let, self,
# class, public, import, as, while, else, return, if, plus // and /* */
# comments. It does not know unsafe, void, null, or the lowercase primitives
# (int, uint, usize, double, char), which simply render unstyled.
*.g linguist-language=Swift
*.g linguist-detectable=false

# The VS Code extension is tooling built around the language, not the language
# itself; left detectable it would make Gata read as a TypeScript project.
editors/** linguist-vendored

# .gconf is an XML project file; Linguist has no mapping for the extension, so
# it renders as plain text. Borrow the XML grammar for highlighting only.
*.gconf linguist-language=XML
*.gconf linguist-detectable=false
